            <ArticleTitle>An Obstructing Small Bowel Phytobezoar in an Elderly Female Nigerian: A Case Report and Literature Review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6962876</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2017/6962876</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Small bowel obstruction secondary to phytobezoars is an unusual presentation in surgery. We present a case of an elderly female patient with an insidious onset of abdominal pain, abdominal distension, and bilious vomiting diagnosed radiologically to be small bowel obstruction. Exploratory laparotomy revealed a trapped mass of vegetable matter in the distal ileum. She had enterotomy with primary closure for removal of obstructing ileal phytobezoars. Her postoperative recovery was uneventful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
